                       SERVICE AGREEMENT
================================================================

Reference:        {{ reference_id }}
Date of Agreement: {{ agreement_date }}

----------------------------------------------------------------

1. PARTIES

1.1 Client ("the Client")

   Name:                       {{ client.legal_name | default("[client name not supplied]") }}
   Type:                       {{ client.entity_type | default("[entity type not supplied]") }}
   Jurisdiction of incorporation: {{ client.jurisdiction | default("[jurisdiction not supplied]") }}
   Registered address:         {{ client.address | default("[address not supplied]") }}
   Registration / company no.: {{ client.registration_number | default("[reg no. not supplied]") }}
   Authorised signatory:       {{ client.signatory_name | default("[name]") }}, {{ client.signatory_title | default("[title]") }}

1.2 Contractor ("the Contractor")

   Name:               {{ contractor.full_name | default("[contractor name not supplied]") }}
   National Identity Card No.: {{ contractor.nic | default("[NIC not supplied]") }}
   Tax Identification Number (TIN): {{ contractor.tin | default("[TIN not supplied]") }}
   Address:            {{ contractor.address | default("[address not supplied]") }}
   Bank account for payment: {{ contractor.bank | default("[bank not supplied]") }}, Account No. {{ contractor.account | default("[account no. not supplied]") }}

   The Contractor is a tax resident of Sri Lanka.

2. SCOPE OF SERVICES

2.1 The Contractor shall provide the following services to the Client (the "Services"):

   {{ services_description | default("[services description not supplied]") }}

2.2 The Services shall be performed by the Contractor in Sri Lanka unless the Parties agree otherwise in writing. The Parties acknowledge that the Services are rendered wholly, exclusively and necessarily for the production of the Contractor's income from the trade or business of the Contractor within the meaning of section 6 of the Inland Revenue Act No. 24 of 2017 (as amended).

2.3 The Contractor shall determine the means, methods and tools of performance and is not subject to the day-to-day control of the Client as to manner of execution.

3. TERM AND RENEWAL

3.1 This Agreement shall commence on {{ start_date | default("[start date]") }} and continue until {{ end_date | default("[end date]") }} (the "Initial Term"), unless terminated earlier under clause 11.

3.2 Renewal:
{% if renewal_variant == "B" %}
   This Agreement shall renew for successive periods of {{ renewal_period | default("one (1) month") }} unless either Party gives written notice of non-renewal at least {{ renewal_notice_days | default("30") }} days before the end of the then-current term.
{% else %}
   This Agreement shall terminate at the end of the Initial Term unless the Parties execute a new written agreement.
{% endif %}

4. COMPENSATION

4.1 In consideration of the Services, the Client shall pay the Contractor:
{% if fee_structure_variant == "B" %}
   An hourly rate of {{ currency | default("LKR") }} {{ hourly_rate | default("[rate]") }} per hour of Services performed, payable on the basis of invoices delivered under clause 5.
{% elif fee_structure_variant == "C" %}
   Such amounts as are set out in Schedule A against each deliverable accepted by the Client.
{% else %}
   A fixed sum of {{ currency | default("LKR") }} {{ monthly_fee_amount | default("[amount]") }} per calendar month.
{% endif %}

4.2 Currency. All sums payable under this Agreement are denominated in {{ currency | default("LKR") }}. Where the currency is not Sri Lankan Rupees (LKR), conversion to LKR for the purposes of Sri Lankan taxation shall be at the Central Bank of Sri Lanka selling rate prevailing on the date the funds reach the Contractor's Sri Lankan bank account.

4.3 Expenses. The {{ expenses_borne_by | default("Contractor") }} shall bear the expenses set out in Schedule B (which may include equipment, software subscriptions, internet, training, business travel, co-working space).

5. INVOICING AND PAYMENT TERMS

5.1 The Contractor shall issue invoices to the Client on a {{ invoice_cadence | default("monthly") }} basis.

5.2 Each invoice shall be payable within {{ net_days | default("30") }} days of issue by electronic transfer to the Contractor's Sri Lankan bank account specified in clause 1.2.

5.3 Foreign-exchange and bank charges. Where the Client is a foreign company, the Client shall bear all originating-bank and intermediary-bank charges; the Contractor shall bear the receiving-bank charges. Any FX margin between the Central Bank of Sri Lanka selling rate and the credited rate shall be borne by the Contractor as a cost of doing business (a deductible business expense under section 6 IRA).

5.4 Late payment. Sums unpaid more than {{ late_days | default("14") }} days after due date shall accrue interest at {{ late_interest_rate | default("1.5") }}% per annum, compounded monthly, until paid.

6. CONTRACTOR STATUS -- INDEPENDENT CONTRACTOR

6.1 The Parties agree and acknowledge that:

   (a) the Contractor is an independent contractor and not an employee, partner, agent, joint-venturer or franchisee of the Client;

   (b) nothing in this Agreement creates an employment relationship, and the Contractor shall not be entitled to any benefits the Client extends to its employees (including EPF/ETF where the Client is a Sri Lankan entity);

   (c) the Contractor is solely responsible for filing the Contractor's own income tax returns and for the payment of income tax and any other taxes due on the Contractor's income from this Agreement;

   (d) where Sri Lankan withholding tax is applicable under sections 83 to 85 of the Inland Revenue Act, the Client shall withhold and remit such tax to the Inland Revenue Department and provide the Contractor with the appropriate WHT certificate.

7. EQUIPMENT, PREMISES, AND EXPENSES

7.1 The Contractor shall provide and maintain at the Contractor's own cost the equipment, software, internet, telecommunications and workspace required to perform the Services, except as set out in Schedule B.

7.2 The Parties acknowledge that the cost of such equipment, software, internet and workspace is incurred by the Contractor wholly and exclusively for the production of the Contractor's income from this Agreement and is therefore deductible under section 6 IRA from the Contractor's assessable income.

8. CONFIDENTIALITY

8.1 Each Party shall keep confidential all information of the other Party received in connection with this Agreement, except where disclosure is required by law, court order, or a competent tax authority (including, for the avoidance of doubt, disclosure by the Contractor to the Inland Revenue Department in support of the Contractor's tax filings).

8.2 This clause shall survive termination of this Agreement for {{ confidentiality_survival_years | default("2") }} years.

9. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

9.1 Intellectual-property treatment:
{% if ip_variant == "B" %}
   The Contractor retains ownership of all intellectual property created under this Agreement and grants the Client a non-exclusive, perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free licence to use such intellectual property for its internal business purposes.
{% elif ip_variant == "C" %}
   Pre-existing intellectual property of either Party (developed independently of this Agreement) remains the property of that Party. Work product created specifically for the Client under this Agreement vests in the Client on payment.
{% else %}
   All work product created by the Contractor specifically for the Client under this Agreement shall vest in the Client upon payment in full of the fees relating thereto. The Contractor assigns to the Client, with effect from the date of such payment, all intellectual property rights in such work product.
{% endif %}

10. WARRANTIES AND LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

10.1 The Contractor warrants that the Services will be performed with reasonable care and skill consistent with industry standards.

10.2 Except for breaches of confidentiality, intellectual property obligations, or gross negligence or wilful misconduct, neither Party's liability under this Agreement shall exceed the total fees paid or payable in the {{ liability_cap_months | default("6") }} months preceding the event giving rise to the claim.

10.3 Neither Party shall be liable for indirect, consequential, special or exemplary damages.

11. TERMINATION

11.1 Either Party may terminate this Agreement by giving {{ termination_notice_days | default("30") }} days' written notice to the other Party.

11.2 Either Party may terminate this Agreement immediately on written notice if the other Party (a) commits a material breach not remedied within {{ cure_period_days | default("14") }} days of written notice; (b) becomes insolvent, files for bankruptcy or has a winding-up petition presented against it.

11.3 On termination, the Client shall pay all undisputed sums due to the Contractor up to the effective date of termination within {{ final_payment_days | default("14") }} days.

12. DISPUTE RESOLUTION AND GOVERNING LAW

12.1 Governing law and forum:
{% if governing_law_variant == "B" %}
   This Agreement is governed by the law of Sri Lanka. Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be finally settled by arbitration under the Arbitration Act No. 11 of 1995 in Colombo, in the English language, before a single arbitrator.
{% elif governing_law_variant == "C" %}
   This Agreement is governed by {{ chosen_law | default("[chosen law]") }}. Disputes shall be referred to arbitration under the {{ arbitration_rules | default("[arbitration rules]") }} in {{ arbitration_seat | default("[seat]") }}.
{% else %}
   This Agreement is governed by the law of Sri Lanka. The Parties submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Colombo.
{% endif %}

12.2 Before commencing any proceedings, the Parties shall first attempt to resolve the dispute by good-faith negotiation for not less than 30 days.

13. GENERAL

13.1 Notices. Notices shall be in writing, delivered to the addresses in clause 1 (or by email to {{ client.notice_email | default("[client email]") }} and {{ contractor.notice_email | default("[contractor email]") }}), and shall be deemed received 2 business days after dispatch.

13.2 Force majeure. Neither Party shall be liable for delay or failure caused by events beyond its reasonable control, including without limitation acts of God, fire, flood, civil unrest, government action, currency restrictions, or telecommunications outage. The affected Party shall give prompt notice and shall use reasonable efforts to mitigate.

13.3 Severability. If any provision is found unenforceable, the remainder of this Agreement remains in force.

13.4 Entire agreement. This Agreement (and its Schedules) is the entire agreement between the Parties on its subject matter and supersedes all prior understandings.

13.5 Counterparts and electronic signatures. This Agreement may be executed in counterparts (including by electronic signature under the Electronic Transactions Act No. 19 of 2006), each of which is an original and all of which together constitute one instrument.

13.6 Amendments. Amendments shall be in writing signed by both Parties.

